RQ("CZ8","P6","What is the main idea of the passage?",["A daily brisk walk is a free and simple habit with many health benefits","Walking is better than every sport","Busy people have no time for exercise","Walking needs special shoes and a partner"],"Every sentence supports the value and ease of a daily walk. ‘Better than every sport’ is extreme; the last option contradicts the passage.");
RQ("CZ8","P7","What is the main idea of the passage?",["The shift from joint to nuclear families has brought both gains and losses","Joint families were always better than nuclear families","Young couples in cities do not want privacy","Elderly people prefer to live alone"],"The passage gives a gain (privacy, freedom) and a loss (the elderly alone) — a balanced main idea.");
RQ("CZ8","P8","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Falling costs have made solar power a growing and promising source of energy in India","India has the sunniest weather in the world","Farmers in India no longer need electricity","Storage batteries have already become very cheap"],"The passage explains why solar power is now cheap, how it is used and how it could grow.");
RQ("CZ8","P8","Which is the most suitable title for the passage?",["The Rise of Solar Power in India","Farmers and Their Fields","The Cost of Batteries","Why Villages Have No Power"],"Solar power’s growth is the topic of every sentence; the other titles are details or wrong.");
RQ("CZ8","P9","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Checking a message before forwarding it can prevent the harm done by false rumours","Phones should be banned to stop rumours","Everyone who forwards a rumour is wicked","Rumours never lead to violence"],"The passage describes the harm of rumours and ends with the remedy: pause and check the source.");
RQ("CZ8","P10","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Millets, once neglected, are winning back their place because of their benefits","Rice and wheat are unhealthy grains","Millets grow only on dry land","Lifestyle diseases are caused by eating rice"],"The passage tells of millets’ decline and return, and gives the reasons — water and health.");
RQ("CZ8","P11","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Online classes during the pandemic showed how unequal access to technology is","Village schools are better than city schools","Laptops are better than phones for study","Schools should stay online for ever"],"The contrast between city and village students leads to the final point about fair access.");
RQ("CZ8","P12","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Public libraries are valuable to everyone but are often neglected","Libraries should charge for entry","Successful people never use libraries","Old books are better than new ones"],"The passage praises what libraries offer and ends with their lack of funds — value and neglect together.");
RQ("CZ8","P13","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Winter haze keeps returning because its causes are not tackled","Schools should be closed every winter","The air in north Indian cities is clean in winter","Children are not affected by the haze"],"The passage lists the causes and victims and ends by blaming short-term steps that leave the causes untouched.");
RQ("CZ8","P14","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Chandrayaan-3’s low-cost landing near the Moon’s south pole was a proud achievement for India","The soil of the Moon is the same as the Earth’s","Space missions abroad are a waste of money","Young Indians are not interested in space"],"The landing, its low cost, its data and the national pride all form one achievement.");
RQ("CZ8","P14","Which is the most suitable title for the passage?",["A Proud Landing near the Lunar South Pole","The Soil of the Earth","Costly Space Projects Abroad","The History of the Moon"],"The passage is about the landing and what it meant; the others are details or outside it.");
RQ("CZ8","P15","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Traditional hand weaving may die out unless its work is fairly valued","Machine-made sarees are better than handmade ones","Young people dislike living in villages","Each handmade saree takes only a day to make"],"The passage ends with its point: without a fair price, the skill may be lost.");
RQ("CZ8","P16","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Computer tools can help doctors read X-rays but should assist, not replace, them","Computers will soon replace all doctors","X-rays are no longer needed in hospitals","Doctors make more mistakes than computers"],"The passage weighs the benefit and the risk and settles on ‘an assistant rather than a replacement’.");
RQ("CZ8","P17","What is the main idea of the passage?",["The new ‘smart’ parking system has made a simple task needlessly complicated","Smart parking has solved the town’s traffic problems","Everyone in the town owns a smartphone","The vegetable market has closed down"],"The long list of steps for a ten-minute stop, and the people who ignore it, show the system complicates parking; the last line is ironic.");
RQ("CZ8","P18","What is the main idea of the passage?",["The printing press made books common and helped ideas spread widely","Hand-copied books were better than printed ones","Gutenberg was the first person in Europe to read","Historians dislike modern inventions"],"Before and after printing: rare books became common, and ideas and reading spread.");
RQ("CZ8","P18","Which is the most suitable title for the passage?",["How Printing Changed the World","The Beauty of Hand-Copied Books","The Life of a Historian","Why Books Are Costly Today"],"The passage is about the effect of printing; the other titles are not its subject.");
RQ("CZ8","P19","What is the main idea of the passage?",["Mangroves protect coasts and support livelihoods, yet they are being destroyed","Fish farms are the best use of coastal land","Mangroves grow only along rivers far from the sea","Storms never reach coastal villages"],"The passage gives the value of mangroves and then the damage done by clearing them.");
RQ("CZ8","P20","What is the main idea of the passage?",["The unpaid flood relief work of young volunteers showed their spirit of service","Floods strike every district every year","College students should never miss classes","The volunteers were paid well for their work"],"The students’ work, its cost to them and the closing line all point to the spirit of service.");

