/* CZ10 — inference */
RQ("CZ10","P1","What can be inferred from the passage?",["Before the pits, much rooftop rain was doing little to refill the groundwater","Rainwater harvesting works only in very large cities","The housing societies no longer need any water from outside","Most drains in Indian towns are badly built"],"The pits ‘send it back into the ground’ and raise well levels, so the lost rain was not refilling the ground before. ‘No water from outside’ goes too far — they buy ‘fewer’ tankers.");
RQ("CZ10","P2","The author would most likely disagree with which statement?",["A complete ban on devices is the best answer for children","Some videos can help children learn","Late-night screen use can be harmful","Parents should help choose what children watch"],"The author says the task is ‘not to ban devices’; the other three statements match the passage.");
RQ("CZ10","P3","What does the passage suggest about zero before it was treated as a number?",["It had served mainly to mark an empty place","It was completely unknown everywhere","It was thought to be the largest number","It was used only by Arab scholars"],"‘Zero as a number, and not merely an empty place’ implies that it had earlier served as an empty place.");
RQ("CZ10","P4","What does the author suggest about the bans on plastic bags announced so far?",["They have achieved little because they are not followed","They have solved the problem completely","They were never needed","They were meant only for big cities"],"Bans ‘announced many times’ but ‘quietly ignored’ suggest they have achieved little.");
RQ("CZ10","P5","It can be inferred that before mobile payments became common, small shopkeepers:",["had to keep plenty of change for their customers","never went to the bank","did not accept money at all","lost money to fraudsters every day"],"Mobile payments mean ‘less need to keep change’, so shopkeepers needed more change before.");
RQ("CZ10","P6","What does the passage suggest?",["Lack of time or money is a weak excuse for not exercising","Only athletes should walk every day","Walking daily can harm the heart","Sports are a waste of time"],"A walk ‘costs nothing’ and is the ‘easiest habit a busy person can build’, so neither money nor a busy life rules it out.");
RQ("CZ10","P7","The passage implies that in joint families, elderly people:",["received daily company and care from their relatives","lived in separate houses","had more privacy than young couples","moved to cities for work"],"The elderly now miss ‘the daily company and care that the old system offered’ — so they had it before.");
RQ("CZ10","P8","What does the passage suggest is still holding solar power back in India?",["The cost of batteries to store the power","A lack of sunshine in India","The high price of solar panels","Farmers’ refusal to use solar pumps"],"‘If storage batteries become cheaper too’ implies that batteries are costly now. Panels have become cheap, and sunshine is plentiful.");
RQ("CZ10","P9","The author thinks that most people who spread false messages:",["mean well but act carelessly","are criminals who should be jailed","know that the messages are false","read every message carefully first"],"They are ‘not wicked’ and think they are ‘warning their friends’, yet they skip ‘a moment’s pause’ — good intentions, careless action.");
RQ("CZ10","P10","The passage suggests that many families gave up millets because of:",["fashion rather than nutrition","a shortage of millet seeds","a ban by the government","the poor taste of millets"],"They chose rice and wheat because these ‘seemed more modern’, though millets are rich in fibre and minerals.");
RQ("CZ10","P11","It can be inferred that during the pandemic many village students:",["missed parts of their lessons","learned more than city students","had faster internet than city students","did not need any lessons"],"One phone for three or four children and a weak network mean that many could not follow every lesson.");
RQ("CZ10","P12","The author would most likely support:",["more money for public libraries","closing down old libraries","selling the books in libraries","charging students for using libraries"],"The author praises libraries and regrets that they are ‘short of funds’.");
RQ("CZ10","P13","How does the author regard the closing of schools for a few days?",["As a step that does not solve the real problem","As the best long-term solution","As the main cause of the haze","As a step that has ended the haze"],"It is called ‘short-term’, and the haze ‘returns every year’.");
RQ("CZ10","P14","What does the passage imply?",["A large budget is not the only key to success in space","India spends more on space than any other country","No country will land on the Moon again","The mission sent back no data"],"The mission cost ‘far less’ yet succeeded, ‘showing what careful planning can achieve on a modest budget’.");
RQ("CZ10","P15","The author suggests that young people leave weaving mainly because:",["it does not earn them enough","they cannot learn the old designs","the looms are too heavy to use","towns have better weather"],"Cheap machine-made copies and the call for ‘a fair price’ show that weaving pays too little.");
RQ("CZ10","P16","The author would most likely agree that:",["doctors and computer tools work best together","computer tools should be banned from hospitals","doctors should stop reading X-rays","crowded hospitals need no new tools"],"‘Used as an assistant rather than a replacement, the technology may save many lives.’");
RQ("CZ10","P17","What does the author really think of the new parking system?",["It has not made parking any simpler","It is the best thing to happen to the town","It should be copied in every town","It is too cheap to be useful"],"The last line is ironic: after five steps for a ten-minute stop, and with many drivers ignoring it, the system has not made life simpler.");
RQ("CZ10","P18","It can be inferred that before printing:",["fewer people could read","everyone owned many books","ideas spread faster than they do today","books were cheap to buy"],"After printing ‘more people learned to read’, so fewer could read before.");
RQ("CZ10","P19","The passage suggests that clearing mangroves may also:",["hurt fishing families in the long run","increase the number of young fish","make the coast safer from storms","help hold the soil in place"],"Mangroves shelter young fish that later support fishing families; removing them removes that shelter.");
RQ("CZ10","P20","The author suggests that good work done by young people:",["often goes unreported","is always rewarded with money","is found only in cities","is less useful than paid work"],"The spirit of service is alive ‘even when it rarely makes the news’.");

/* CZ11 — vocabulary in context */
RQ("CZ11","P1","The word ‘upkeep’, as used in the passage, means:",["maintenance","the cost of building","official permission","special training"],"‘Needs little upkeep’ — little looking after or maintenance.");
