RQ("CZ11","P5","The word ‘common’, as used in the passage, means:",["widespread","vulgar","jointly owned","cheap"],"Paying by phone has become widespread. ‘Vulgar’ and ‘jointly owned’ are other senses of ‘common’ that do not fit.");
RQ("CZ11","P6","The word ‘brisk’, as used in the passage, means:",["quick and energetic","slow and relaxed","long and tiring","lonely"],"A brisk walk is a fast, lively one.");
RQ("CZ11","P6","Which word is most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘brisk’ as used in the passage?",["sluggish","rapid","lively","healthy"],"Brisk means quick and energetic; its opposite is ‘sluggish’. ‘Rapid’ and ‘lively’ are synonyms.");
