RQ("CZ11","P8","The word ‘sharply’, as used in the passage, means:",["steeply","harshly","cleverly","clearly"],"The cost ‘has fallen sharply’ — steeply and quickly. ‘Harshly’ fits ‘spoke sharply’, not a fall in price.");
RQ("CZ11","P9","The word ‘wicked’, as used in the passage, means:",["evil","clever","lazy","unlucky"],"‘Not wicked’ — not evil; they mean well.");
RQ("CZ11","P9","Which word is most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘prevent’ as used in the passage?",["cause","stop","avoid","delay"],"To prevent harm is to stop it; the opposite is to cause it. ‘Stop’ and ‘avoid’ are close in meaning.");
RQ("CZ11","P10","The word ‘humble’, as used in the passage, means:",["simple and ordinary","shy","respectful","poor in quality"],"‘These humble grains’ are simple, everyday ones. The passage praises them, so ‘poor in quality’ is wrong; ‘shy’ and ‘respectful’ describe people.");
RQ("CZ11","P10","Which word is most nearly OPPOSITE in meaning to ‘scarce’ as used in the passage?",["plentiful","rare","dirty","costly"],"Water growing scarce means there is less and less of it; the opposite is ‘plentiful’. ‘Rare’ is a synonym.");
